  "body": "## Summary\n\n* **Goal:** keep screen-maintenance options in one place with a short explanation.\n* **What changes:** **Settings → Display → Screen Cleaning**, with **Refresh Frequency** and **Sunlight Fading Fix** moved there. Saved values, JSON keys and web settings stay compatible; Sunlight Fading Fix keeps its board restrictions. No refresh behavior changes.\n\n| Display | Screen Cleaning | Refresh Frequency |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ![Display](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MikalaiKryvusha/crosspoint-reader/pr-assets/07-screen-cleaning/cleaning-display-en.webp) | ![Screen Cleaning](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MikalaiKryvusha/crosspoint-reader/pr-assets/07-screen-cleaning/cleaning-menu-en.webp) | ![Refresh options](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MikalaiKryvusha/crosspoint-reader/pr-assets/07-screen-cleaning/cleaning-options-en.webp) |\n\n## Scope Check\n\n- [x] I have read SCOPE.md and ROADMAP.md.\n- [x] This PR is **not** a new built-in theme.\n- [x] This PR is **not** a new external network connector.\n- [x] This PR is **not** an interactive app, writing tool, RSS/news/browser, media playback, or PDF feature.\n- [x] The stock firmware does not already handle this well, **and** no other popular CrossPoint fork already does.\n- [x] This PR does not touch `freeink-sdk/`, `lib/hal/`, the bootloader, OTA, or recovery code.\n\n## Additional Context\n\n* On branch commit `ea0a3625`, `default` (C3), `x4pro-gh_release` and the simulator builds passed. In English and Russian: open the submenu, change Refresh Frequency, check the saved value, Back through Display → Settings → Home.\n* This PR provides the submenu. **#4376 adds Refresh Images and Refresh Sleep Screen** with optional one-time delayed redraws to reduce traces of previous screens. Its description shows the combined menu and delay controls.\n\n---\n\n### AI Usage\n\nDid you use AI tools to help write this code? _**YES**_\n",
